{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he led them with bread.</b> He led them gently, in the manner of עָלוֹת יְנַהֵל (Isaiah 40:11). He gave them bread little by little, to eat but not to satiety, as is proper in years of famine, as they said (Ta'anit 11a): one who keeps himself hungry in years of famine is saved from unusual death. And the medical authorities have already said that satiety after famine causes fatal illness." "<b>In that year.</b> After the money was exhausted — and it was the sixth year of the famine."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:59.671614729Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}